<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  RUSH scenario: a high-speed weaving showcase.

  The env raises the lane speed limit to 50 m/s at reset() (see
  laneiq/env/highway_env.py). The ego vType (maxSpeed 50) can then
  outrun every background vehicle, which stay capped at their own
  maxSpeeds:

    aggressive 40 m/s · normal 33.33 m/s · slow 25 m/s · ego 50 m/s

  So the ego is uniquely the fastest car on the road. This route
  file supplies a LOW-density traffic stream (the standard 60/25/15
  normal/aggressive/slow mix) — sparse enough that the fast ego has
  room to actually use its speed and weave cleanly, rather than
  charging into a wall of traffic.

  Total arrival rate ~0.30 veh/s (≈ the low-density file). At 50 m/s
  the ego's closing speed onto slow traffic is high (up to 25 m/s),
  so a busy road made the problem unlearnable — the first attempt
  (ppo_v6) thrashed. Lowering the density gives the policy room to
  spot slow vehicles early and change lanes with margin.

  Born out of the Week-8 request for a demo that shows the agent
  threading high-speed through traffic; the gauntlet (LESSONS #15)
  handles the start-stuck case, rush handles the outrun-everyone case.
-->
<routes xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://sumo.dlr.de/xsd/routes_file.xsd">

    <route id="r_through" edges="e1"/>

    <!--
      Slow-heavy mix, no aggressive cars. Every vehicle the ego catches
      is strictly slower than it (normal 33, slow 25 vs ego cap 50), so
      cruising behind one costs real speed reward and overtaking pays.
      We also push the slow flow into ALL lanes (departLane="best")
      rather than concentrating it in lane 0 — so the ego has to pick
      the clearest lane at each obstacle, not just escape one lane.
    -->
    <flow id="f_normal"     type="normal"     route="r_through"
          begin="0" end="3600" period="exp(0.10)"
          departLane="best" departSpeed="desired"/>

    <flow id="f_slow"       type="slow"       route="r_through"
          begin="0" end="3600" period="exp(0.20)"
          departLane="best" departSpeed="desired"/>

</routes>
